{{\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Self-Test
\par}
{\tc\tcl4 \v Self-Test}
In order to support CMVP, the library implements Self-Test functionality that is available with all compilation options. The test is always performed as part of library initialization (power-up). There is no conditional self-test functionality as none of such conditions occur (i.e. pair-wise consistency test, software/firmware load test, manual key entry test, continuous random number generator test, and bypass test).\par
If the self-test fails the manager enters a {\b fail-closed}  error state: {\f2 {\b imb_get_errno()}}  returns {\f2 {\b IMB_ERR_SELFTEST}} , the {\f2 {\b IMB_FEATURE_SELF_TEST_PASS}}  feature flag is cleared and all job, burst and direct APIs on that manager are disabled - they return {\f2 NULL} /{\f2 0} /{\f2 -1} , do not produce any output and report {\f2 {\b IMB_ERR_SELFTEST}} . {\f2 {\b imb_ml_kem_new()}}  and {\f2 {\b imb_ml_dsa_new()}}  return {\f2 {\b IMB_ERR_SELFTEST}} , and all operations on ML-KEM/ML-DSA contexts created earlier with that manager (except {\f2 {\b imb_ml_kem_free()}} /{\f2 {\b imb_ml_dsa_free()}} ) return {\f2 {\b IMB_ERR_SELFTEST}}  as well. Status/query APIs ({\f2 {\b imb_get_errno()}} , {\f2 {\b imb_get_strerror()}} , {\f2 {\b imb_get_features()}} , {\f2 {\b imb_get_flags()}} , self-test callback APIs) and {\f2 {\b free_mb_mgr()}}  remain functional. A subsequent successful {\f2 init_mb_mgr_*()}  call on the same manager restores normal operation.\par
Application can register self-test callback function to track test progress. Optionally application can corrupt input message for selected tests and observe change in the test result.\par
Example sequence of callbacks received by an application is:{
\par
