{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
API to get error status. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Error status is kept per {\b IMB_MGR}; when {\i mb_mgr}  is not NULL and its status is set, that value is returned. Since an {\b IMB_MGR} is owned by a single thread this makes the status thread specific. When {\i mb_mgr}  is NULL, or the manager has no error recorded, a process wide status is returned instead. That fallback is shared by all threads and can be overwritten by another thread's API call, so it is only reliable for APIs that do not take an {\b IMB_MGR} (e.g. {\b alloc_mb_mgr()}). Always pass the manager used for the failing call when one exists.\par
