{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
\par
{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Automatically initialize most performant Multi-buffer manager based on CPU features. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Manager initialization and the power-up self-test.\par
Every init_mb_mgr_*() call runs the library self-test (see IMB_FEATURE_SELF_TEST and IMB_FEATURE_SELF_TEST_PASS). If the test fails the manager enters a fail-closed error state:{
\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
{\b imb_get_errno()} returns IMB_ERR_SELFTEST and IMB_FEATURE_SELF_TEST_PASS is cleared in the feature flags;\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
every job, burst and direct API on that manager is disabled: calls return NULL / 0 / -1 as appropriate, do not write to any output buffer and set IMB_ERR_SELFTEST;\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
{\b imb_ml_kem_new()} and {\b imb_ml_dsa_new()} return IMB_ERR_SELFTEST, and every operation on ML-KEM/ML-DSA contexts created earlier with that manager (other than {\b imb_ml_kem_free()}/imb_ml_dsa_free()) returns IMB_ERR_SELFTEST;\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
{\b imb_get_errno()}, {\b imb_get_strerror()}, {\b imb_get_features()}, {\b imb_get_flags()}, {\b imb_self_test_set_cb()}/imb_self_test_get_cb() and {\b free_mb_mgr()} remain functional. The application should check {\b imb_get_errno()} after initialization. A subsequent successful init_mb_mgr_*() call on the same manager restores normal operation. \par}
